## Add a new enemy type
1) Define template in `EnemyTemplateManager` (type, HP, behaviors).
2) Implement movement/attack behaviors if new; export parameters.
3) Ensure bullets spawn through `EntityFactory`; connect signals safely.
4) Add to a wave via `WaveDefinition` or stage JSON/CFG if applicable.
5) Play-test; cap bullet counts; verify cleanup and pooling.

## Add a new stage or wave
1) Create `StageDefinition` and `WaveDefinition` resources.
2) Use formation helpers; validate counts and defaults.
3) Register stage in `StageTemplateManager` (only registered stages are traversed).
4) Test progression and boss entry; ensure stage loops if fewer stages exist.

## Add a new boss
1) Define boss template + phases; use data-driven phase behaviors.
2) Ensure behaviors are added directly (not deferred) once boss is in-tree.
3) Hook defeat into `EventBus` and stage progression.

## Tweak bullet readability
1) Adjust bullet shaders/settings via exported parameters.
2) Consider glow/trails sparingly; keep performance in mind.
3) Validate readability across ranks and screen shake.

## Connect a signal safely
1) Check signal existence and prevent duplicates with `is_connected()`.
2) Use `Callable(self, "method_name")`; disconnect on cleanup/reuse.
3) Guard handlers with `is_instance_valid()` and safe dictionary/array access.

## Add a pooled bullet/enemy type
1) Add pool registration via `EntityFactory` with limits and defaults.
2) Expose spawn params via templates/config; avoid hardcoding.
3) Validate reuse path: visibility toggle, signal disconnect, state reset.

## Validate stage/wave data
1) Run resource/JSON validators; supply safe defaults on missing fields.
2) Ensure `StageTemplateManager` registration for traversal.
3) Test under MAX bullet caps; confirm graceful degradation.

## Quick debug checklist (non-intrusive)
1) Gate logs; prefix with system (e.g., `[StageController]`).
2) Verify node validity before use; re-check after `await`.
3) Reproduce with minimal scene; profile allocations per frame.